speechtext:
Motion No. 7.
That Bill C-113 be amended in Clause 18 by striking out line 38 at page 7 and lines 1 to 3 at page 8 and substituting the following therefor:
"ment exists where any of the following circumstances applied to the claimant:".
Motion No. 8.
That Bill C-113 be amended in Clause 18 by striking out lines 31 and 32 at page 8 and substituting the following therefor:
"(n) formal promise of increase in wages or salary that was not fulfilled;
(o)	unjustified reduction in wages or salary;
(p)	loss in wages or salary due to employer's financial difficulties;
(q)	wages or salary that are less than provided for by legislation;
(r)	intolerable working conditions;
(r) unreasonable work requirements;
(t)	moral objections to employer's practices that are contrary to professional ethics, the law or regulations;
(u)	moral objections to employer's illegal activities or employer's activities that violate freedom of conscience;
(v)	place of work distant from family and serious sickness in the family;
(w)	exertion by employer of excessive pressures to retire;
(x)	working conditions that, in the opinion of a medical practitioner, adversely affect the person's health;
(y)	working conditions considered, on credible and convincing explanations by the claimant, as adversely affecting the claimant's health;
(z)	long period of separation from family due to distance of place of work from family residence;
(ad) moving because of impending marriage;
(bb) decision to start a business or to become self-employed;
(cc) ceasing to act as strike-breaker;
(dd) refusal by employer to grant leave of absence for incapacity to work due to a difficult pregnancy;
(ee) refusal to grant leave of absence to take care of any adopted child;
(ff) need to attend a course of instruction on the recommendation of the Commission;
(gg) refusal to perform job duties on grounds of objections based on religious beliefs;
(hh) failure to re-enlist for a further term of service in the Canadian Forces;
(ii) abusive treatment from co-workers;
(jj) serious or unsolvable transportation problems;

March 19, 1993
Government Orders
(kk) in the case of a minor, having to move with parents;
(It) intolerable living conditions related to employment, particularly with respect to accommodation, food or other physical aspects;
(mm) disciplinary action that is clearly disproportionate; and (nn) such other circumstances as are reasonable."
